  "body": "PR139 established that the prior GeomNode scan and six cached stages omitted a separate procedural terrain source route. This adds one bounded runtime diagnostic at the original Road7 CPU-read boundary: actual terrain node, camera rgb/TERRAIN tag state, cached shader sources/overrides, known24input bindings and owner texture metadata.\n\nCPU candidate projections and four level0 texels use read-only memoryviews of already resident buffers. No full image copy, GPU request/readback, extra render/task, runtime setter or model. CPU states and candidate samples never prove actual cull/draw/driver uniforms/pixel ownership, depth ties or repair. All inherited frozen runtime, source-image, budget and lifecycle gates remain intact. Original matrix3/4PASS, overallFAIL, Stage7=false.\n\nValidation:19new math/window tests and12new snapshot/receiver tests;111focused regressions and actionlintPASS. One fresh independent review and exact full sourceCI precede one request-only native execution; actual evidence and final exactHEAD verification follow.\n\nStacked on Draft PR139. No main merge or environment/registry publication.\n",
